-- Per-species overworld display size for the PMDCollab sheets (national dex -> scale,
-- 1.0 = the sprite's own size). Generated by tools/generate_pmd_scale.py with
--     --metric blend --floor 0.49 0.8 12 27
-- i.e. each species is sized so its PMD art is as big as its HGSS sprite is after
-- lib/HGSS_scale.lua (the mean of the height and the area), but never below a pixel-density
-- floor that rises from 0.49 (small species) to 0.8 (big ones), so a large Pokemon is not
-- shrunk into a tiny, too-fine sprite. Species without both sprites stay at 1.0.
-- Then softened toward the middle, like lib/HGSS_scale.lua: each drawn height d became
-- 18 * (d / 18) ^ 0.65 px (smallest ~10 px, biggest ~40 px; it was ~8 to ~62), then the
-- small ones lifted again: below 18 px, 18 * (d / 18) ^ 0.75 (smallest ~12 px).
-- Hand-tune any value; lib/hd_field.lua applies it (with the gen3-hd-sprites library and
-- Species Sizes on) about the sprite's ground point. A form
-- is sized like its base species; a form key ("479-heat") sizes one form on its own.
